    <item>
      <title>Psychological Science Podcasts</title>
      <link>http://scchen.com/post/ps-podcasts/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 17 May 2021 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://scchen.com/post/ps-podcasts/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;There are psychological scientists who have started producing internet podcasts since 2016. Audience will know the latest news and ideas because many hosts are open science promoters. Until now 8 podcasts are in my pocket. They are the treasure for those who want to know the true faces of scientists. Two days ago I completed the Chinese version. I wish scientific podcasts outside of English will be online in coming months.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;1-everything-hertz&#34;&gt;1. Everything Hertz&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hosts: James Heathers, Dan Quintana
Channels: 
&lt;a href=&#34;https://everythinghertz.com/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Website&lt;/a&gt;, 
&lt;a href=&#34;https://twitter.com/hertzpodcast&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Twitter&lt;/a&gt;
Debut: 2016&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;2-the-black-goat&#34;&gt;2. The Black Goat&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hosts: Simine Vazire, Alexa Tullett
Channels: 
&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.theblackgoatpodcast.com/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Website&lt;/a&gt;, 
&lt;a href=&#34;https://twitter.com/blackgoatpod&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Twitter&lt;/a&gt;
Debut: 2017&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;3-circle-of-willis&#34;&gt;3. Circle of Willis&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Host: Stuart Ritchie
Channels: 
&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.circleofwillispodcast.com/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Website&lt;/a&gt;, 
&lt;a href=&#34;https://twitter.com/circleofwillis&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Twitter&lt;/a&gt;
Debut: 2018&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;4-the-road-to-open-science&#34;&gt;4. The Road to Open Science&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Host: Malte Elson
Channels: 
&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.malte-elson.com/podcast/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Website&lt;/a&gt;, 
&lt;a href=&#34;https://twitter.com/road2openscience&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Twitter&lt;/a&gt;
Debut: 2018&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;5-two-psychologists-four-beers&#34;&gt;5. Two Psychologists Four Beers&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hosts: Alexa Tullett, Yoel Inbar
Channels: 
&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.fourbeers.com/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Website&lt;/a&gt;, 
&lt;a href=&#34;https://twitter.com/four_beers&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Twitter&lt;/a&gt;
Debut: 2017&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;6-the-bayes-factor&#34;&gt;6. The Bayes Factor&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Host: Daniel Lakens
Channels: 
&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.bayesfactor.nl/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Website&lt;/a&gt;, 
&lt;a href=&#34;https://twitter.com/bayesfactorpod&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Twitter&lt;/a&gt;
Debut: 2020&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;7-reproducibiliteapod&#34;&gt;7. ReproducibiliTeaPod&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Host: Various ReproducibiliTea organizers
Channels: 
&lt;a href=&#34;https://soundcloud.com/reproducibilitea&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Website&lt;/a&gt;, 
&lt;a href=&#34;https://twitter.com/reproduciteapod&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Twitter&lt;/a&gt;
Debut: 2019&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;8-physiology--behavior-podcast&#34;&gt;8. Physiology &amp;amp; Behavior podcast&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Host: Psychology &amp;amp; Behavior journal
Channels: 
&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.journals.elsevier.com/physiology-and-behavior/podcast&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Website&lt;/a&gt;
Debut: 2020&lt;/p&gt;
